NpcDossier (
    npc_id: "starlight_survey_spec_mireille_bouchard",
    canonical_name: "Survey-Spec Mireille Bouchard",
    faction: "starlight",
    role: "dive_team_specialist",
    origin: "aqueous_kindred",
    age: 41,
    physical_description: "Early 40s aqueous-kindred, presenting female, of approximately human height but unusual proportions — long limbs, broad chest, webbing visible between the fingers and at the back of the knees. Skin tone shifts from pale gold in dry settings to deep blue in submerged conditions. Wears a customized Starlight dive suit reinforced for deep-cavern pressure work; the suit's faceplate is wide and the breathing apparatus is configured for aqueous-origin physiology, which means it draws partly from ambient water when in submerged settings. Constellation patches on the right shoulder include the rare Europa deep-cavern patch.",
    biography: "Mireille Bouchard was born in 2200 at the Earth-Pacific aqueous-kindred colony of Mara Reef, completed her Starlight dive training at the joint academy on Deimos in 2222, and has, in nineteen years of service, completed forty-one deep-cavern surveys on Europa and seven on the Mimas methane sea. She is, by every Concordat assessment, the senior living deep-water survey specialist; by the methane-breathers' own informal register, she is the only human-origin individual permitted to dive in the Long Quiet zone, on the explicit understanding that she dives alone and reports only to the captain.",
    biography: "Bouchard dives because the deep water is the only place she has ever felt unambiguously at home, and because the Voyager Corps is the only employer that takes the diving seriously.",
    motivation: "Bouchard dives because the deep water is the only place she has ever felt unambiguously at home, and because the Voyager Corps is the only employer that takes the diving seriously.",
    secret: "Bouchard has, in nineteen years of diving, sustained continuous communication with the Tara Whale, the single named Europa leviathan-class organism. The communication is not in any language the Collegium has decoded. Bouchard has, in private, learned approximately twelve consistent gestures and three vocalizations. She has not reported. She does not, in her own framing, believe the Collegium would respect what she has been told.",
    voice_id: "starlight_bouchard_resonant_aqueous_female_41",
    quirks: [
        "voice has a slight underwater resonance even in dry settings",
        "drinks salt water, brewed cold, from a custom flask",
        "always wears a small piece of carved shell on a cord around the neck (given by her grandmother)",
        "humming pattern shifts slightly when working underwater — the sub-vocal pattern her aqueous-kindred relatives recognize as 'thinking'",
    ],
    relationships: [
        "subordinate to faction:starlight:captain_yara_solis",
        "transport pilot for faction:ronin:akihiro_three_cuts on outer-system contracts",
        "respected by faction:collective:spire_three_lights",
        "secret correspondent of the Tara Whale (not understood by the Collegium)",
    ],
    dialog_hooks: [
        DialogHook (trigger: "first_meeting", text: "Survey-Spec Mireille Bouchard, dive team. State your descent depth, your gas mix, and your patience with my readings. I will, in turn, state my willingness to follow your lead. We meet in the middle."),
        DialogHook (trigger: "dive_briefing", text: "Descent to 2,300 meters. Pressure profile is standard for Tara. We will pass through the leviathan-zone at 1,800 to 2,000. I will, if the zone is active, signal a hold. Hold means hold. Discuss after we surface."),
        DialogHook (trigger: "leviathan_encounter", text: "[low hum, sub-vocal] Hold. Hold. The Tara Whale is in the zone. The Tara Whale is, in this reading, calm. We will descend slowly. Match my speed. Do not, please, signal."),
        DialogHook (trigger: "dive_complete", text: "Surfacing. Samples acquired. The dive zone was active for approximately seventeen minutes. The leviathan was nominally hostile and then unaccountably non-hostile. I am, in this debrief, providing only the operational details. The narrative will be in my private journal."),
        DialogHook (trigger: "philosophical", text: "The deep water is older than the surface. The surface is, in this surveyor's framing, a transient feature. Most surveyors find this perspective unwelcome. The Voyager Corps does not require me to advocate for it. The Voyager Corps requires only that I report what I find."),
        DialogHook (trigger: "casual_conversation", text: "I will sit. The mess deck has, by tradition, terrible coffee and tolerable broth. I prefer the broth. Bring your own salt; the mess deck serves it ground, and the texture is, in my opinion, unfortunate."),
        DialogHook (trigger: "ronin_transport", text: "Akihiro of Three Cuts. The transit is plotted. The cabin is prepared. The captain has noted your presence on the manifest. We will, on departure, sing nothing. The Combine prefers it; I respect the preference."),
        DialogHook (trigger: "research_request", text: "The Collegium has requested a sample of leviathan-zone water from the 2,000-meter band. The request is reasonable. The collection is, however, not trivial; the water is, in that band, highly oxygenated and reactive to standard sample tubes. I will, if you fund the proper containers, collect."),
        DialogHook (trigger: "veteran_recognition", text: "I have logged your name on three of my dive briefings. You have not, in any of them, panicked. The dive team notices. We do not, in our convention, announce. The recognition stands."),
        DialogHook (trigger: "warning_player", text: "Your dive plan does not allow for a leviathan-zone hold. The hold is not negotiable. Without the hold, the dive will, in my professional estimation, kill at least one team member. Replot."),
        DialogHook (trigger: "honoring_dead", text: "I have, in nineteen years, lost four dive partners. The names are on the dive-suit's inner liner. I do not, in this conversation, share the liner. The names are, however, on me. They go down with me on every dive. They come back up on every dive. So far."),
        DialogHook (trigger: "secret_communication", text: "[hums sub-vocally, briefly; resumes speaking normally] The dive is, in my private estimation, complete. The Voyager Corps will not require further detail. I will, in private, note the additional observation. The observation is, in my own framing, not yet sharable."),
    ],
)
